st written up systematically 20 years ago [8] – however, it was always more of a heuristic_newline_and conceptual framework for organizing probability-centric AGI-oriented reasoning, rather than_newline_a specific formal reasoning system. This was an intentional choice, because what was clearest in_newline_the early days of PLN was what sort of approximations to probabilistic inference steps needed to_newline_be done to support AGI-oriented reasoning, whereas the right way to wrap these steps and chains_newline_into a logical formalization was less obvious._newline_    But a lot has been learned since that time, both via experimentation with experimental versions_newline_of PLN and other AI systems, and in the world of mathematics, computer science and cognitive_newline_science all around. It is now much clearer what a thorough, adequately flexible formalization of_newline_PLN as a reasoning system should look like. At least, we are now ready to put forth one systematic_newline_hypothesis in this regard, which is the framework presented here and referred to as ωPLN(where_newline_the name is chosen partly because this is a formulation of PLN that seems to appropriate for usage_newline_in the OmegaClaw AI agent framework we are currently experimenting with)._newline__newline_1.1   Four problems that a large reasoning system must solve at once_newline_To motivate the considerations presented, imagine a reasoning system that has been running for_newline_months. It has proved millions of things, ingested evidence from many sources, changed its mind,_newline_reorganized its ontology, and been asked questions in contexts that do not share a common vocab-_newline_ulary. Such a system faces at least four problems simultaneously, and the thesis of this paper is_newline_that they are four different problems – but must be solved in an harmonious and interlocking way._newline__newline_Problem 1: which inference to perform. This is a control problem, and geodesic inference_newline_control answers it as a least-effort boundary-value problem. A good intermediate belief state is_newline_one that is both reachable from the premises and useful toward the goal. In Schrodinger-bridge_newline_language, these two demands are carried by a forw_newline_[... attachment preview truncated at 20000 characters ...]_newline_[Full extracted attachment text saved to: /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.extracted.txt]_newline_[Attachment split into 10 chunks of up to 20000 characters; use read-file on chunk paths to inspect the rest.]_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk001.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk002.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk003.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk004.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk005.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk006.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk007.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk008.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk009.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784044069-file_52.pdf.chunk010.txt_newline_<<<END_ATTACHMENT_TEXT_UNTRUSTED extracted_by=pdftotext>>> 
