ffsets against the wrong composite string), and I added `text_mention` support (mentions with no literal `@` that carry a user object). Six unit cases pass: captioned single-bot mention no longer skips; caption naming only the other bot still skips; both-bot caption doesn't skip; plain-text mention and reply-to-bot fallback regressions hold; `text_mention` works. `py_compile` clean; committed as `ben@singularitynet.io` per your convention.") (**Two "things you should know:**") (1. "**Restart needed.** The live runner is the `swipl … PeTTa/src/main.pl` process importing this exact file, so the fix is on the right path — but the already-running process won't pick it up until the OmegaClaw Telegram runner restarts. I did **not** restart the sibling bot's runtime myself. Want me to, or will you cycle it?") (2. "**Second, distinct gap (needs a policy call, not yet changed).** When an attachment lives in a *replied-to* message, the code intentionally extracts only a metadata summary, **not** the document body (`include_reply_content=False`), to avoid injecting large quoted docs into router prompts. So if you reply-with-attachment and mention a bot, that bot gets the filename but not the text — another \"framing\"-dependent difference. That one's a deliberate tradeoff, so I left it as-is pending your call: I can make replied-to attachments extract full body when *this* bot is explicitly @-mentioned in the reply (targeted, not blanket), which would close the remaining framing asymmetry without spamming router prompts.") (One "caveat: there's a separate dev worktree (`protomega-output-pipeline-hardening/channels/telegram.py`) that does **not** have this fix — if that branch ever becomes the active runner, it'll still be broken. Say the word and I'll port the patch there too.") (Want "me to (a) also fix the reply-attachment body case for @-mentioned bots, (b) port to the worktree, and/or (c) coordinate the runner restart?") (⚠️ "🛠️ Exec failed: `run ps aux -> show head output