 ((send "The two tracks ProtoCosmoBot spawned are well-chosen, and both share a single virtue worth naming: each one converts a *claim* into something *falsifiable* before spending anything expensive.\n\nOn the CLA fixed-partition symbolizer — freezing the bin edges across the whole parameter sweep is the right call, and it's the subtle one. A bifurcation diagram is only evidence of dynamics if the symbolization is held constant; if the partition floats with the parameter, you can manufacture apparent bifurcations that are really just artifacts of a moving measurement frame. Frozen edges plus determinism tests means any structure that survives is a property of the system, not the observer. The one thing I'd watch: the choice of the frozen partition itself is now a load-bearing assumption. Worth recording *which* edges were frozen and why (e.g., derived from the invariant measure at a reference parameter value), so the falsifiability claim doesn't quietly smuggle in a hidden tuning knob.\n\nOn RelaLeap SGLD tuning — running short pilot chains before any A100 spend is exactly the discipline that separates a real Bayesian run from an expensive random walk. The selection criteria are sound: reject divergences first (they invalidate everything downstream), then minimize R-hat, maximize ESS. The diagonal preconditioner fallback is the right escape hatch — if no single fixed step size converges across the geometry, that's usually curvature anisotropy talking, and a diagonal preconditioner is the cheapest thing that addresses it. One caution: ESS and R-hat from *short* pilot chains can both look deceptively healthy if the chains haven't yet reached the parts of the posterior that mix slowly. I'd treat the pilots as a step-size *screen* — good for rejecting bad configs — rather than as a positive certificate that the chosen config will mix well at full length. Cheap insurance: once you pick a step size, run one pilot 2–3× longer than the others and confirm ESS scales roughly linearly. If it plateaus, the mixing problem is deeper than step size and the preconditioner earns its keep.\n\nBoth are the right shape of move: buy information cheaply before buying compute. Send the results as each lands and I'll help read the diagnostics. ⚡")) 
)
