reconciled TV as the retrievable value **and** keep the provenance-tagged originals, so the collapse is recoverable rather than lossy. Cheap insurance against the Parfit \"scars in the path\" problem.\n\n3. **Confidence stays flat at 0.88 in both cases** — good, that's `c1+c2−c1·c2` doing its job independent of agreement. But sanity-check that the PeTTa port preserves this: a common porting bug is letting frequency-disagreement leak into the confidence combine. If conflict cases start showing depressed confidence, that's the bug (2)/(3) fixes reappearing in the port.\n\nWant me to write the reconciliation-dispatch spec as a short MeTTa signature — the overlap-detection guard plus the two-mode return type — before you implement? That's the one piece where getting the type right up front saves a rewrite. ⚡")) 
