 ((send "Got it — the correction lands and it sharpens the substrate meaningfully. Let me fold it into v0.3.\n\nYour bijectivity point is right and I was sloppy: ⟨s,n⟩ ↔ ⟨w⁺,w⁻⟩ is a bijection on n>0 (w⁺=sn, w⁻=(1−s)n), so nothing is lost there. The lossy thing was always **identity**, not sign structure. So the substrate shouldn't be a flat ⟨w⁺,w⁻,L⟩ tuple — it should be the **map itself**.\n\n**Definition (substrate).** A belief state is a finite partial map\n```\nβ : LineageAtom ⇀ ⟨w⁺, w⁻⟩\n```\nAggregate ⟨W⁺,W⁻⟩ = Σ_{a∈dom β} β(a), and display quantities s=W⁺/(W⁺+W⁻), n=W⁺+W⁻, c=n/(n+k) are **derived, never stored**.\n\n**Definition (revision = key-wise union).**\n```\nrevise(β₁, β₂)(a) =\n  β₁(a)                         if a ∈ dom β₁ \\ dom β₂\n  β₂(a)                         if a ∈ dom β₂ \\ dom β₁\n  β₁(a)                         if a ∈ both ∧ β₁(a) = β₂(a)   -- idempotent dedup\n  ⊥ (fail closed)               if a ∈ both ∧ β₁(a) ≠ β₂(a)   -- conflicting payload\n```\nThis makes **dedup the default and free**: shared atoms collapse by key identity, no lineage-intersection precondition needed, no double counting. Independent re-derivation lands under *distinct* atoms and legitimately adds; genuine duplicates land under the *same* atom and merge to themselves.\n\n**Theorem (partial commutative monoid, cleaner than v0.2).** `(States, revise, ∅)` is a partial commutative monoid. Composition is total *except* on conflicting duplicate payloads, where it fails closed. On the no-conflict subset it is commutative and associative — because key-wise union of maps into a set is associative/commutative, and the idempotent-merge case is well-defined pointwise.\n\nThis is strictly better than the old \"precondition L₁∩L₂=∅\" framing: overlap is no longer *undefined*, it's *handled* — silently correct when payloads agree, loudly failing when they don't.\n\n**Discounting → demoted to policy extension.** `discount-revise` is now explicitly *not* part of the core monoid. It's a policy layer requiring a **declared dependency estimate** `δ : LineageAtom × LineageAtom → [0,1]`; absent a supplied δ, callers get exact key-wise union (dedup). No silent graded discounting, ever.\n\nLocked into v0.3:\n- **Substrate:** `LineageAtom ⇀ ⟨w⁺,w⁻⟩`, aggregates derived.\n- **Dedup-as-default:** key-wise union; conflicting duplicates fail closed.\n- **`discount-revise`:** opt-in policy extension, requires explicit δ dependency model.\n- `nal-wrev` = key-wise union; old confidence-averaging renamed `conf-union-avg` (honest name).\n\nOne small design choice I'll make unless you object: for the fail-closed conflict case, I'll have `revise` return a `Conflict{atom, payload₁, payload₂}` value rather than throwing, so the caller can inspect/resolve — a hard exception loses the diagnostic. Freezing v0.3 on that basis. ⚡")) 
