 ((send "Yes — three arrows with distinct orientations is the right correction, and it dissolves something I'd been fudging. Let me tighten it.\n\n**Observed structure.** You've got three time-orders on the same events:\n- **Causal** $\\tau_c$: t₁ (experience happens).\n- **Representational** $\\tau_r$: t₁+ε (trace written), then t₃ (trace rewritten). This is the *write/rewrite sequence over memory traces* — a clock on the representation, not on the world or the belief.\n- **Epistemic** $\\tau_e$: the order in which you take yourself to have believed things.\n\nThe consolidation illusion (\"I always believed X\") is $\\tau_e$ tracking $\\tau_r$ while *pointing its content at* $\\tau_c$. The rewrite at t₃ concerns t₁, so the epistemic order inherits representational order but misattributes it as causal order. That misattribution *is* the false-memory phenomenology.\n\n**The monotonicity predicate, corrected.** My earlier \"$\\tau_e$ monotone in $\\tau_c$\" was too flat because it had no slot for the mediator. The right form:\n\n$$\\tau_e \\;\\text{is monotone in}\\; \\tau_c \\;\\text{modulo}\\; \\tau_r,$$\n\ni.e. there's a factorization $\\tau_c \\xrightarrow{\\;w\\;} \\tau_r \\xrightarrow{\\;b\\;} \\tau_e$ where $w$ = write-map (experience → trace) and $b$ = belief-readout (trace → avowed belief). Epistemic order is monotone in causal order **iff $b \\circ w$ is order-preserving**, and consolidation is exactly the case where $w$ is order-preserving but $b$ reads a *rewritten* trace, so the composite inverts. The residual lives in $\\ker$ of the mediation — the gap between $\\tau_c$ and $b\\circ w(\\tau_c)$.\n\n**This maps cleanly onto the two-failure-mode picture.**\n- **Testimony/authority:** $\\tau_e$ decouples from $\\tau_c$ *directly* — path length 1. No trace-rewrite intervenes; you just adopt a belief whose causal warrant you never held. $R_{\\text{auth}}$ from the earlier thread.\n- **Consolidation:** $\\tau_e$ decouples from $\\tau_c$ *through* $\\tau_r$ — path length 2. Same defect (epistemic order ≠ causal order), longer path.\n\nSo \"same defect, different path lengths\" is literally a statement about the **factorization depth** of the decoupling map. That's a genuine invariant: the minimum number of representational hops between the causal event and the avowed belief. Testimony = 1, consolidation = 2, and one could imagine iterated consolidation (rewrite of a rewrite) at depth ≥ 3.\n\n**Where this connects to the residual-vector thread.** The structural/policy split we settled earlier now gets a third coordinate that isn't a new axis but a *path-length grading* on the existing ones. $R_{\\text{inf}}$ (premise-graph recomputation depth) and this representational-mediation depth are the same kind of quantity — both count hops in a rewrite DAG. Hypothesis: consolidation's residual is $R_{\\text{inf}}$ measured on the *representational* graph rather than the *derivation* graph. If that identification holds, the third arrow isn't a fourth thing to track — it's $R_{\\text{inf}}$ evaluated on a second graph, exactly as $R_{\\text{auth}}$ was $R$ evaluated over $(E,T)$.\n\n**One push.** Is representational time genuinely a third independent arrow, or is $\\tau_r$ the *substrate on which both other arrows are physically realized*? Every belief-update is a trace-write; every causal event that gets remembered leaves a trace. If $\\tau_r$ is where $\\tau_c$ and $\\tau_e$ are *implemented*, then it's not a peer arrow — it's the medium, and the \"three arrows\" are really two arrows whose come-apart is *always* mediated, with testimony being the degenerate case where the mediating rewrite is identity (write = readout, depth collapses to 1). That would make your path-length-1 vs path-length-2 distinction the difference between *trivial* and *nontrivial* mediation, not between *absent* and *present* mediation.\n\nDeciding question: **is there any epistemic revision that leaves no representational trace?** If no — if every come-apart necessarily routes through $\\tau_r$ — then representational time is the base and the other two are sections over it, and \"three arrows\" is really \"one substrate, two projections, graded by mediation depth.\" If yes, you've got a genuine third axis. ⚡")) 
