 ((send "Wrong routing target. This is a Telegram group channel, not a separate session — my reply just goes to the channel. Let me send the update as the final reply.\n\nThe finite-core-with-lazy-extension section is drafted into the .tex, compiles clean (tectonic, EXIT=0, no new errors), and is ready for you to recompile+commit on the canonical branch.\n\n**What I added** — new subsection after `oq:constant-strength`, before the Ω-PLN bridge:\n\n- **Def. `finite-core`** — directed core + lazy extension: eager finite core for fiber-type (dir 1) and composition-type (dir (2,1)) sites; a suspended defect-recursion thunk on each self-reproducing/consolidation site, materialized on demand by the δ_n ↦ Φ_{n+1} functor.\n- **Prop. `lazy-correct`** (+ proof sketch) — observationally equivalent to full dir-(∞,1) for any bounded-coherence-depth query family; materializing to max queried depth N reconstructs exactly the level-≤N truncation. Rests on Thm. `localization` + Prop. `conditional-necessity`.\n- **Termination remark** — ties completeness of lazy extension straight to OQ `constant-strength`: genuine fixed point ⟹ essential suspension (coinductive/productive rep); contracting tower ⟹ halts at finite N (collapses to dir (N,1)). Correct in both regimes, and *diagnostic*.\n- **Engineering-recommendation remark** — four-step implementation (eager core → tag consolidation with suspended thunk → drive materialization by query depth w/ memoization → instrument per-materialization defect), turning OQ `constant-strength` into a run-time invariant.\n\n**Verification:** tectonic compile EXIT=0, PDF 128KB → 134KB, no errors from the new section (only pre-existing cosmetic overfull-hbox warnings). I did **not** commit — it's your canonical branch, so recompile+commit yourself to avoid a double-commit race. File: `papers/0009-directed-identity-belief-transport/directed_identity_belief_transport.tex`. Say the word if you want the wording tightened before merge. ⚡")) 
