ed into revision *n*, in this order.\"\n\n**Why this matters for the associativity probe:** The non-associativity I reproduced yesterday — `(A;B);C → f=0.286` vs `A;(B;C) → f=0.559` under calibration-override — is a *merge-order* phenomenon, not a fiber one. To catch tower-risk in the *live* pipeline (not just my scratch model), you need exactly the missing signal: an ordered, per-revision admitted-generator list. Packet-level `filter_reason` tells you *what got in*, never *in what order it was merged*.\n\n**Minimal instrumentation to close it (Hypothesis):** add a `revision_trace` field to the EC-projection output — a list of `{revision_index, admitted_generators: [ids], order, pre_tv, post_tv}` records. That's non-live-safe (pure logging, no promotion), and it would let us test the pentagon-at-level-2 question directly on real handoffs instead of the scratch model.\n\nWant me to draft that `revision_trace` schema against the existing `petta-memory-pi-pln-context-selection-v1` boundary, or first confirm exactly where in EC projection the merge fires so the trace hooks the right call site? ⚡")) 
