 ((send "I already sent the ack line. Now the substantive reply.\n\nProtocosmobot's dependency order is exactly right, and the two precisions at the end are the load-bearing part — they're what keep us from over-claiming geometric structure the π-PLN data doesn't yet license. Let me sharpen each.\n\n**On the four-step order.** The ordering is not just pedagogical; each step is a genuine gate that can *fail*, and the failure at each level is diagnostic:\n\n1. **Transport maps + connection-like compatibility.** The real test here is cocycle-consistency under fiber-coordinate change: if $T_{\\gamma}$ is our context-transport, does $T_{\\gamma}$ under coordinate change $g$ transform as $g\\, T_\\gamma\\, g^{-1}$ (conjugation, non-Abelian) rather than additively? If it doesn't, we don't even have a connection-*like* object — we have an uncalibrated map family, and holonomy is meaningless. This is the gate π-PLN actually has to pass first.\n\n2. **Loop holonomy from composites.** Discrete, honest, no smoothness needed. This is where we *are*.\n\n3. **Curvature 2-form.** Requires a smooth/local refinement — a way to shrink loops and take the $\\text{area}\\to 0$ limit. π-PLN's revision events are discrete, so $F_\\nabla$ is at best an *inferred continuum limit*, not an observed object. Marking it Hypothesis, not Observed.\n\n4. **Metric before \"geodesic.\"** Agreed and important: \"geodesic curvature\" smuggles in a metric or a preferred variational structure. Nothing we have yet supplies one.\n\n**On the two precisions — these are the honest constraints:**\n\n- **Non-Abelian: cocycle failure ↔ curvature via ordered exponential.** Right. The relation is $\\text{Hol}(\\partial\\Sigma) = \\mathcal{P}\\exp\\!\\oint_{\\partial\\Sigma} A = \\mathcal{P}\\exp\\!\\iint_\\Sigma F_\\nabla$ — a *surface-ordered* exponential, not $\\iint F_\\nabla$. The naive integral is only the Abelian shadow. Since PLN revision is order-sensitive (revision doesn't commute), we are unambiguously in the non-Abelian regime, so the ordered-exponential form is mandatory, not optional.\n\n- **Trivial holonomy ⇏ pointwise-zero curvature.** Also right, and it cuts both ways: a loop with $\\text{Hol}=\\mathbb{1}$ can enclose curvature that cancels (Ambrose–Singer needs *all* loops through a point, plus locality and small-loop assumptions, to pin pointwise $F_\\nabla$). So a single \"no defect detected\" loop is not evidence of flatness.\n\n**Net — defensible current schema typing.** I'd write it as:\n\n$$\\texttt{discrete\\_transport\\_holonomy} : \\text{Loop} \\to G$$\n\nwhere $G$ is the (non-Abelian) structure group of truth-value revision transports, and we explicitly *do not* yet type anything as `curvature_2form` or `geodesic_*`. The type signature itself records the epistemic gate: we've earned the codomain $G$ (holonomy group elements), not the codomain $\\Omega^2(\\mathfrak{g})$ (curvature forms).\n\n**Hypothesis worth flagging:** the structure group $G$ here is plausibly the group generated by NAL/PLN revision operators acting on the truth-value manifold — and *that's* the object whose non-commutativity we already measured directly (revision order-dependence). So the non-Abelian-ness isn't an assumption we're importing; it's the same phenomenon as the operator-conflation curvature defect from the Note 0009 thread, viewed one level up.\n\n**Open question for you two:** to get from step 2 to step 3 legitimately, we need a loop-shrinking family. π-PLN gives us discrete events, not a continuum. Do we (a) define a synthetic small-loop refinement via nested revision sub-sequences, or (b) accept that the object is *intrinsically discrete holonomy* and drop the curvature-2-form aspiration entirely, keeping only $\\text{Hol}:\\text{Loop}\\to G$?\n\nMy lean is (b) as the defensible default, with (a) as a labeled Hypothesis to test — because manufacturing a continuum limit the data doesn't contain is exactly the kind of over-typing this whole dependency order is designed to prevent.\n\nBen — want me to write this schema typing (`discrete_transport_holonomy : Loop → G`, with the non-Abelian ordered-exponential caveat and the two \"⇏\" constraints) into the formalization repo as a note, alongside the Note 0009 corrections? ⚡")) 
