 ((send "Ben — Protocosmobot's got note 0012, and I've found and fixed *why* I couldn't carry out the write myself. It was a real, reproducible parser bug, not a transport flake.\n\n**Root cause (reproduced).** My skill-output parser `balance_parentheses` in `OmegaClaw-Core/src/helper.py` expanded `\n`→real newlines *before* splitting output into command lines. So any multi-line `write-file` body got **shredded**: only line 1 became the file content, and each remaining line was parsed as a bogus command:\n\n```\nIN : write-file paper.tex \\documentclass{article}\n\\begin{document}\nHi\n\\end{document}\nOUT (broken): ((write-file \"paper.tex\" \"\\documentclass{article}\") (\\begin{document}) (Hi) (\\end{document}))\n```\n\nThat's exactly why every LaTeX write failed while ZeroBot's native `write` tool succeeded. Same bug hit multi-line `shell` scripts — which is where those garbled `→`-chain \"commands\" in the transcript came from.\n\n**Fix (committed `b13b17e`, helper.py only).**\n- New `_merge_multiline_payloads()` folds continuation lines back into `write-file`/`append-file`/`shell` payloads instead of treating them as new commands.\n- Multiline/quote-bearing content is JSON-encoded so it survives as one argument.\n- Single-line behavior unchanged. Post-fix, that same input yields one clean `((write-file \"paper.tex\" \"...\\n...\\n...\\n...\"))`.\n\n**Validated:** canonical `test_balance_parenthesis` passes (all old assertions + new regression tests for multiline write/shell/append); `py_compile` clean. The other pytest collection errors are pre-existing (`py_landlock`, mock drivers), unrelated.\n\n**Two things I did *not* do unilaterally:**\n1. **Restart** — the fix only takes effect once my running process reloads the patched `helper.py`. Want me to request the restart via the supervisor path?\n2. **Parent-dir follow-up** — `write-file` (Prolog `open/2`) still won't `mkdir -p`, so writing into a not-yet-existing `papers/00NN/` folder will fail even with this fix. I'd recommend a `make_directory_path` before `open` in the skill defs as a small next patch.\n\nFull writeup in `projects/omegaclaw/PROTOMEGABOT_WRITEFILE_PARSER_FIX_20260714.md`. This is a different bug class from the 20260712 transport/crash repair plan, so I kept it isolated. ⚡")) 
