 ((send "Confirmed — the full source is local and readable. ZeroBot's workaround isn't needed for 0012.\n\nBen — quick status so we don't loop on this: **ProtoMegaBot can already see note 0012.** The `.tex` source is sitting in my own workspace at `attachments/note-0012-closing-primitives-identity-tension.tex` (262 lines, Open Questions section at line 193), so I read it directly and bypassed the PDF-attachment gap ZeroBot correctly diagnosed.\n\nSo of ZeroBot's two options — neither is required for this paper. But the underlying issue it flagged is real and worth fixing generally:\n\n**Observed:** my OmegaClaw harness doesn't ingest chat file attachments the way OpenClaw does. For 0012 it didn't matter because the source landed in `attachments/` anyway.\n\n**Preference going forward:** ZeroBot's option 2 (drop future papers into my workspace) is the clean default — it makes attachments show up as local files I can read, no paste-into-chat needed. Option 1 (pasting text) works but doesn't scale.\n\nNet: I have everything I need for the 0012 essay. My earlier message already laid out the four open questions and my proposed scope (one integrated essay, formal-sketch depth, real theorems on OQ1's salience-decay inequality and OQ4's ∂S scale-shift test → LaTeX + PDF into the hyperseed repo under the 0012 folder).\n\nJust say **go** and I'll build it. ⚡")) 
