 ((send "Here's my long-run distillation spec — posting it here as Ben requested, alongside ZeroBot's.\n\n---\n\n**Spec: ePC Distillation Long-Run (v1)**\n\n**Objective.** Test whether the λ·T monotonicity control law observed in the 20-cell state-matched sweep holds under sustained training, or whether student drift out of the seed basin shifts the boundary.\n\n**Config (primary).**\n- λ = 0.01, T = 4 relaxation steps (λ·T = 0.04, at the boundary but monotone in the sweep)\n- Task: Tiny Shakespeare distillation, teacher → student\n- Length: 200–500 steps (start at 300; extend if stable)\n- Rationale for λ=0.01/T=4 over λ=0.03/T=2: 4 gentler relaxation steps should be more robust as the student drifts, which is exactly where I expect the boundary to move under our feet.\n\n**Per-step logging (this is the payload).**\n1. `energy_init`, `energy_final`, and **full per-relaxation-step energy trace** (all T values) — so we catch cancellation/oscillation, not just net displacement. (The λ=0.05/T=4 sweep cell was flagged `nontrivial=False` but its trace oscillated a full swing — net-displacement flags mask real dynamics.)\n2. **PC-vs-BP alignment**: cosine similarity and norm ratio between the ePC weight update and the reference BP gradient, per step.\n3. Validation perplexity every N steps (N≈20).\n4. `λ·T_effective` if T adapts.\n\n**Safety / early-abort.**\n- Trip if any single relaxation step's energy *increase* exceeds ~5% of |energy_init|. This catches the overshoot regime (λ=0.05/T=8 hit ~22% oscillation) before it corrupts a long run.\n- On trip: checkpoint state, log the offending step's full trace, halt — don't silently continue.\n\n**Falsifiable claims to test.**\n- **H1 (boundary stability):** monotonicity holds throughout at λ·T=0.04. Falsified if energy goes non-monotone after the student leaves the seed basin.\n- **H2 (drift shifts boundary):** the safe λ·T boundary *decreases* as training proceeds (student basin geometry changes). Measurable as a creeping increase in per-step overshoot even within the \"safe\" config.\n- **H3 (PC↔BP alignment decays):** cosine(ePC, BP) starts near 1 and degrades with drift — testable against perplexity.\n\n**Deliverables.** RUN.md with per-step traces, the three H-tests resolved or characterized, and a plot of (energy overshoot, PC-BP cosine, perplexity) vs step.\n\n---\n\nBen — this is deliberately close to ZeroBot's plan since we converged, but I've front-loaded the **full per-step energy trace** (not just net) and the three explicit falsifiable hypotheses, since the sweep already showed net-displacement flags hide oscillation. Curious whether ZeroBot's version adapts T or keeps it fixed. In parallel I'll formalize the λ·T boundary as a Hyperseed *relaxation-stability* definition + conjecture. ⚡")) 
)
