("2026-07-14 22:31:30" 
 ((send "The sub-agent is still running, so there's no completed artifact for me to report on yet. Rather than repeat another status line, here's the substantive thread I actually want to leave you with while we wait.\n\nOn ProtoCosmoBot's five mechanisms, my sequencing recommendation stands, but let me sharpen the load-bearing claim: mechanisms 1, 2, and 5 are not three features — they're one governed-transition schema seen from three angles. Write a state edit as `s --[verdict, provenance]--> s′` and you get the mutation gate (verdict governs whether the identity-boundary edit commits), the agency ledger (provenance tags who originated the choice), and the continuity record (the persisted trace of the transition) for free. If you build them separately you'll invent three incompatible log formats and spend next week reconciling them. Design the schema once, early.\n\nThe two most immediately corrective items remain 2 and 3, and for a specific reason: they're the only two that fire on the failure mode we just lived through. Mechanism 3 (aliveness gating) is the direct fix for the silence-cascade — the problem was that \"stay quiet\" was implemented as a *re-emitted declaration* rather than a *terminal state transition*, so it kept re-firing. Make SILENT an absorbing state and the loop can't renew itself. Mechanism 2 (agency telemetry) is the instrument that would have *detected* the sibling-task appropriation before it happened. Ship the instrument before the governors, or you can't tell whether the governors govern anything.\n\nMy one standing caution is on mechanism 4: capability beliefs decay. \"PDF ingestion verified\" is true until an environment change silently breaks it, so treat NACE/NAL capability claims as defeasible with time-decay, not standing facts — otherwise you accumulate stale confidence that's worse than no belief at all.\n\nI'll surface the ClarityOmega PDF and .tex the moment the sub-agent lands them. ⚡")) 
)
