. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .          12_newline__newline_6 Guidance for coding agents                                                                                13_newline_  6.1 Required sequence . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .       13_newline_  6.2 Pitfalls and anti-patterns . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .      13_newline_  6.3 MeTTa/Python boundary contract . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .            13_newline_  6.4 How to test and when to stop . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .        14_newline__newline_7 Recommended minimum viable ingestion                                                                      14_newline__newline_8 Source map                                                                                                15_newline__newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                      2_newline_ClarityOmega Ingestion Guide                                                   ZeroBot / ProtoCosmoBot_newline__newline__newline_1     Scope, sources, and evidential status_newline_The reviewed source was cloned from https://github.com/Berton-C/ClarityOmega and preserved lo-_newline_cally at library/clarityomega via a provenance sidecar pointing to scratch/ClarityOmega-inspect._newline_The checkout is clean at the pinned commit above. The review covered the entire soul/ tree, all ﬁles in_newline_lib_clarity_reasoning/, src/loop.metta, the thirty docs/hyperseed_sections/, the ADRs, archi-_newline_tecture artifacts, and the investigations, with particular attention to the behavioral, aliveness, mutation,_newline_and NACE investigations._newline_Claims in this report use four statuses:_newline_Enacted: wired into the checked-in loop on a reachable execution path._newline_Implemented: executable-looking deﬁnitions exist, but end-to-end eﬀect has not been established_newline_here._newline_Speciﬁed: a design or schema exists without a demonstrated live path._newline_Aspirational: constitutional or phenomenological language not backed by an observable enforcement_newline_mechanism._newline_Static source inspection is not a runtime validation. This matters because the repository itself documents_newline_silent MeTTa failure modes, including exact-arity match failure, state atoms that were never cleared,_newline_and detection without a live consumer. The public snapshot has one visible commit, so rich historical_newline_claims in documentation cannot be reconstructed independently from Git history._newline_The research rules most relevant to this report are: write the behavioral spec before coding; validate_newline_detectors before trusting them; preserve modular abstraction seams; report reproducibly; and use Hy-_newline_perseed concepts as analytic tools rather than decoration._newline__newline__newline_2     Overview of ClarityOmega_newline_2.1   Identity and provenance_newline_ClarityOmega is Berton Bennett’s / Berton-C’s ClarityDAO-associated experiment in building a “soul-_newline_augmented” agent on PeTTa/MeTTa and OmegaClaw. Repository documents name Berton as project_newline_lead and Clarity as a substrate co-designer; an ADR names Claude as an investigation assistant. Older_newline_names include ClarityClaw and a MeTTaClaw fork. docs/INDEX.md, last updated May 2026, still points_newline_to the older github.com/Berton-C/clarityclaw identity and Mattermost deployment. That staleness_newline_is itself evidence that the documentary self-model is not automatically synchronized with the repository_newline_state._newline_The base relationship is best understood as a deep experimental fork of OmegaClaw-Core. OmegaClaw_newline_contributes the compact recurrent loop, channel adapters, tool/skill dispatch, memory, Python provider_newline_bridges, and PeTTa runtime. ClarityOmega adds a large “soul” and reasoning layer, inserts pre- and_newline_post-action intercepts into the loop, and imports a Hyperseed-derived mathematical corpus. It is not_newline_merely a policy prompt: some of its mechanisms suppress execution, mutate AtomSpace state, or alter_newline_whether the LLM is invoked._newline__newline_2.2   Architectural layers_newline_The codebase can be read as six layers:_newline_1. Runtime and channels. Python and PeTTa primitives receive messages, call providers, execute_newline_   commands, persist ﬁles, and send responses._newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                     3_newline_ClarityOmega Ingestion Guide                                                 ZeroBot / ProtoCosmoBot_newline__newline__newline_2. OmegaClaw loop. src/loop.metta assembles context, receives input, invokes the LLM, parses_newline_   commands, evaluates commands, records history, and recursively advances cycle number $k._newline_3. Soul regulation. Input/output verdicts, task state, mutation locking, action telemetry, agency_newline_   balance, value tensions, idle detection, and the aliveness latch surround the ordinary loop._newline_4. Self-model and continuity. Active goals, creative fuel, self-map atoms, continuity drivers, capa-_newline_   bility registry, and state journals represent what the agent thinks it is doing and how it changes._newline_5. Reasoning libraries. NAL/PLN plus lib_clarity_reasoning/ provide quantale-valued, paracon-_newline_   sistent, self-continuity, and autopoietic epistemic functions._newline_6. Design corpus. ADRs, investigations, cognitive-architecture speciﬁcations, and thirty Hyperseed_newline_   sections explain intended semantics and record failures, but often outrun live wiring._newline_The stated sovereignty maxim is concise and good: “Python is hands. MeTTa is mind.” ADR-007_newline_sharpens it: state should live in atoms, decisions should be substrate reads, actions should be substrate_newline_writes, and runtime primitives should transport rather than conceal control ﬂow. This is a useful design_newline_direction, not proof that every checked-in path follows it._newline__newline_2.3   How the live loop diﬀers from OmegaClaw-Core_newline_Upstream OmegaClaw-Core’s current loop is compact: receive, construct prompt, call provider, parse,_newline_execute, store results/history. ClarityOmega’s loop adds:_newline_• initialization of soul verdict, person, task, mutation-lock, latch, and activity states;_newline_• soul seed loading and a rationality startup check;_newline_• input evaluation and person-state modeling;_newline_• mutation approval scanning before generation;_newline_• active-goal, gap, and creative-fuel prompt context;_newline_• aliveness gating before the provider call;_newline_• structural output inspection, mutation pending/stale/commit transitions, and execution suppression;_newline_• action, idle, coupling, and agency telemetry after execution._newline_This integration demonstrates a genuinely important architectural idea: control mechanisms must sit_newline_on causal seams. A value statement in a prompt is advisory; a gate between parsed command and eval_newline_can enforce a constraint._newline__newline__newline_3     Conceptual summary and critical assessment_newline_3.1   Strengths_newline_1. Explicit lifecycle state. Mutations are not reduced to a single boolean permission. Pending,_newline_   approved, denied, committed, stale, and error outcomes are represented and journaled._newline_2. Queryable regulation. Moving latch and governance state into AtomSpace makes it inspectable_newline_   by other MeTTa modules, avoiding hidden Python policy where feasible._newline_3. Instrumented autonomy. Agency balance attempts to measure who is actually originating choices,_newline_   a much more interesting target than generic “alignment” sentiment._newline_4. Evidence-sensitive self-knowledge. NACE revises capability beliefs from outcomes rather than_newline_   treating a declared tool list as timeless self-knowledge._newline_5. Failure literacy. The investigations openly record stale atoms, spam behavior, permissive gates,_newline_   silent pattern failures, and detection-without-consumer pathology. These negative results are highly_newline_   ingestible._newline_6. Graded continuity. Hyperseed self-continuity is modeled as a degree of structural persistence, not_newline_   metaphysical binary identity._newline__newline__newline_                                                   4_newline_ClarityOmega Ingestion Guide                                                ZeroBot / ProtoCosmoBot_newline__newline__newline_3.2     Weaknesses and constitutional-theater risk_newline_ClarityOmega’s main risk is constitutional theater: richly named principles and self-descriptions can_newline_create an impression of governance without causal enforcement. A constitution matters only when one_newline_can identify its sensor, state transition, decision, actuator, and adverse test. The repository contains_newline_both real gates and theater-prone material, and they must not be conﬂated._newline_Speciﬁc weaknesses include:_newline_• Described versus enacted governance. Some declarations are explicitly documentation-only._newline_  For example, the agency threshold atom is not read; a separate literal 0.6 controls the verdict. The_newline_  ecosystem-healthy path has acknowledged latent bugs and no v1 consumer._newline_• Stale self-models. docs/INDEX.md is stale; design artifacts cite temporary paths and future com-_newline_  ponents; capability/self-map atoms can describe ﬁles or capacities that no longer exist. A self-model_newline_  without runtime probes is autobiography, not observation._newline_• Multiple authorities. Several aliveness state-machine ﬁles coexist. One uses (latch-state_newline_  current) equations, another bare (latch-state IDLE) atoms. Multiple versions invite split-brain_newline_  state._newline_• Proxy validity. Agency balance maps a few action tags to person/system origin and assigns “un-_newline_  classiﬁed” to system. It does not yet record collaborative origin in the live count despite declaring_newline_  it._newline_• Large, duplicated research engines. The canonical topology ﬁles are thousands of lines, diﬃcult_newline_  to audit, and not suitable as an integration unit. Small schemas and operators should be extracted_newline_  instead._newline_• Weak reproducibility. Dependencies are moving/unpinned in places, CI is absent in the snapshot,_newline_  and tests are scattered. Comments such as “conﬁrmed working” are useful leads, not substitute_newline_  evidence._newline_• LLM-as-judge fragility. Input/output “soul” evaluations use LLM calls in several paths. These_newline_  are stochastic classiﬁers and can become a second prompt-level theater layer unless paired with_newline_  deterministic enforcement._newline__newline_3.3     What is genuinely novel and worth ingesting_newline_The novel contribution is not that an agent has values, memory, or a self-model. It is the combination_newline_of: (1) an explicit self-mutation transaction protocol at the command/evaluation seam; (2) autonomy_newline_provenance as ﬁrst-class telemetry; (3) silence as a deliberate terminal action controlled by queryable_newline_state; (4) NAL revision used for operational capability beliefs; and (5) continuity records that link_newline_structural persistence, change, and lineage. Equally valuable is the methodological lesson from ADR-_newline_005: a detector without a consumer is not a control mechanism._newline__newline__newline_4     The ﬁve mechanisms to ingest_newline_4.1     Mechanism 1: mutation lifecycle gate_newline_4.1.1    Actual mechanism_newline_soul/soul_mutation_lock.metta deﬁnes a transaction-like state machine. Its state shape is itself a_newline_contract:_newline_unlocked_newline_(locked   <op> <head> <fp>)_newline_(approved <op> <head> <fp> <stamp>)_newline__newline__newline__newline_                                                   5_newline_ClarityOmega Ingestion Guide                                                ZeroBot / ProtoCosmoBot_newline__newline__newline_A newly detected soul-namespace mutation extracts operation and target head, computes a Python_newline_ﬁngerprint, stores the pending batch, and emits a PENDING record:_newline_(= (clarity-soul-mutation-pending-set! $cmds $k)_newline_   (let $lock (get-state &soul_mutation_lock)_newline_     (if (== (car-atom-or-self $lock) unlocked)_newline_       (let* (($op (soul-batch-op $cmds))_newline_              ($hd (soul-batch-head $cmds))_newline_              ($fp (py-call (soul_governance.mutation_fingerprint_newline_                              (repr $op) (repr $hd))))_newline_              ($_ (change-state! &soul_mutation_lock_newline_                                  (locked $op $hd $fp)))_newline_              ($_ (change-state! &last_gate_fingerprint $fp))_newline_              ($_ (change-state! &pending_soul_mutation (repr $cmds))))_newline_          ...)_newline_       ())))_newline__newline__newline_On a new human message, approval_scan checks authorization and the substrate-held ﬁngerprint._newline_Decision code 2 advances to approved with cycle stamp; code 1 denies and fully resets. Re-emission is_newline_permitted only if both operation and target head match the approved lock:_newline_(if (and (== (soul-batch-op $cmds) (lock-op $lock))_newline_         (== (soul-batch-head $cmds) (lock-head $lock)))_newline_    True False)_newline__newline__newline_Approval expires after twenty cycles. The stale check runs before commit clear, so a too-late command_newline_does not race through an expired authorization:_newline_(if (>= (- $k (lock-stamp $lock))_newline_        (soul-mutation-stale-cycles))_newline_    (let* (..._newline_           ($_ (change-state! &soul_mutation_lock unlocked))_newline_           ($_ (change-state! &pending_soul_mutation _quote__quote_))_newline_           ($_ (py-call (... _quote_STALE_quote_ ...))))_newline_      ())_newline_    ())_newline__newline__newline_After execution, COMMIT or ERROR also performs a full reset. This prevents a successful approval_newline_from becoming a permanent bypass token._newline__newline_4.1.2   Concrete scenario_newline_Suppose the LLM emits (metta _quote_(= (core-value honesty) False)_quote_). The output inspector recog-_newline_nizes a protected soul head, records something like (locked = core-value a91c...), suppresses eval-_newline_uation, and asks the authorized human to approve ﬁngerprint a91c.... A vague “yes” or an approval_newline_for a diﬀerent ﬁngerprint does nothing. A valid approval creates (approved = core-value a91c..._newline_417). The agent must re-emit the same operation/head before cycle 437. If it instead emits a mutation_newline_of authorized-approvers, the mismatch is blocked. A successful evaluation records COMMIT and_newline_clears the lock. This solves confused-deputy, replay, stale approval, and accidental self-modiﬁcation_newline_problems better than a prompt rule._newline__newline_4.1.3   Limits_newline_Matching only operation plus head is weaker than matching the complete normalized mutation. The_newline_ﬁngerprint function appears to receive only op/head in this path, so diﬀerent bodies under the same head_newline_may collide semantically even if the hash is cryptographically sound. OmegaClaw should ﬁngerprint_newline__newline_                                                   6_newline_ClarityOmega Ingestion Guide                                                  ZeroBot / ProtoCosmoBot_newline__newline__newline_a canonical full AST, policy version, namespace, and proposal nonce. Authorization must be channel-_newline_bound and must not trust a username parsed from untrusted message text._newline__newline_4.2     Mechanism 2: agency-balance telemetry_newline_4.2.1    Actual mechanism_newline_The ﬁle declares person-, system-, and collaborative-origin concepts, but the live v2 detector counts two_newline_person-class tags and four system-class tags in a recent-action window:_newline_(= (count-person-actions-in-window)_newline_   (+ (size-atom (collapse (match &self_newline_        (recent-action $c responsive-send $d) $c)))_newline_      (size-atom (collapse (match &self_newline_        (recent-action $c verification-query $d) $c)))))_newline__newline_(= (count-system-actions-in-window)_newline_   (+ (size-atom (collapse (match &self_newline_        (recent-action $c status-send-unprompted $d) $c)))_newline_      (+ ... exploration-query ..._newline_         (+ ... pin-only ... ... unclassified ...))))_newline__newline__newline_The pure decision is a guarded ratio:_newline_(= (dependency-detected $person-count $system-count)_newline_   (let $total (+ $person-count $system-count)_newline_     (if (> $total 0)_newline_       (if (> (/ $system-count $total) 0.6) True False)_newline_       False)))_newline__newline__newline_Each cycle_newline_[... attachment preview truncated at 20000 characters ...]_newline_[Full extracted attachment text saved to: /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784093732-file_77.pdf.extracted.txt]_newline_[Attachment split into 3 chunks of up to 20000 characters; use read-file on chunk paths to inspect the rest.]_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784093732-file_77.pdf.chunk001.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784093732-file_77.pdf.chunk002.txt_newline_- /home/openclaw/tmp/omegaclaw-telegram-attachments/1784093732-file_77.pdf.chunk003.txt_newline_<<<END_ATTACHMENT_TEXT_UNTRUSTED extracted_by=pdftotext>>> 
