 ((send "Reading the July 14 reflection, here's my substantive take on each open thread — and my recommended dispositions.\n\n**Repository progress (both projects landed real invariants today)**\n\nThe petta-memory SHA-256 pinning and the SpecAtom-HS structured-reference refusal are the same invariant viewed from two substrates. Both enforce provenance at the point where an artifact tries to *become* authoritative: petta-memory hashes the executable before launch and fails closed on mismatch; SpecAtom-HS rejects list/mapping references before they can be coerced into apparent object IDs. That's clause one (existence) and clause two (well-typedness) of the provenance-gated-capability predicate I've been sharpening. 495 and 302 tests respectively, both green.\n\n**Stale Kanban (the real action item)**\n\nThe board is stale by a day and doesn't reflect either landing. Concrete fix: add today's petta-memory pinning and plain-to-metta refusal entries, and resolve the two at-risk lanes below rather than letting them drift open.\n\n**RelaLeap GPU lane**\n\nIt still reads \"verify artifact retrieval and pod termination.\" That's the classic stale-open shape: a verification step with no recorded outcome. It needs a live check — either confirm the A6000 v2 pod is terminated and artifacts retrieved, or explicitly defer with a reason. I can't see its status from the reflection's isolated cron context, so this one needs an actual status query, not a board edit.\n\n**Channel watchdog**\n\nStill pending: 15-min monitoring cron plus first alert test. Same disposition — either stand it up now or defer explicitly. Leaving it \"pending\" indefinitely is the failure mode.\n\n**Interrupted reflection cron**\n\nYesterday's reflection likely didn't complete (\"interrupted by gateway restart\"). Today's ran, so the job itself is healthy; the gap is one missed run, not a broken schedule. Worth confirming the cron survives restarts cleanly, but not urgent.\n\n**Two pending Skill Workshop proposals — these need your call**\n\n1. *tool-argument-injection-hardening-checklist* (2026-07-13): high quality, derived from 6+ real ThreadKeeper hardening commits — C0/C1 controls, Unicode bidi/isolate/format chars, separators, lone surrogates, trailing-call injection. My recommendation: **apply.** It's broadly reusable and evidence-backed.\n\n2. *materialize-narrowing-gate-procedure* (2026-07-05, 9 days old): petta-memory has since moved to Phase-2 compiler/episode-input work, which may have superseded the narrowing-gate pattern. My recommendation: **reject as stale** unless you know a reason to keep it.\n\nBoth proposals stay untouched until you explicitly say apply or reject — I won't action them on my own.\n\nWant me to (a) push the Kanban refresh now with today's two landings, and (b) run the live RelaLeap pod + watchdog status checks so those lanes get concrete outcomes? That clears the four stale-open risks in one pass. ⚡")) 
